WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:05.279
There have been scenes of jubilation in Mali,
after France said it would begin to pull its

00:00:05.279 --> 00:00:07.710
troops out of the West African country.

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:12.220
France has helped in the struggle against
radical Islamic militias for nine years - until

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:15.400
relations with Mali's military leaders turned
sour.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:20.550
Paris objects to their alleged hiring of a
Russian mercenary group to fight the jihadists.

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:25.270
But for now there's a sense of relief in Bamako.

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:33.100
In the streets of Bamako, Malians wave brooms
and sweep away ash - symbolising the departure

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:38.629
of French troops after nearly a decade.

00:00:38.629 --> 00:00:43.329
French President Emmanuel Macron announced
the withdrawal of anti-jihadist forces on

00:00:43.329 --> 00:00:49.120
Thursday - after months of escalating tensions
with Mali's military leaders.

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:54.340
But his inital timeline of four to six months
is now under question.

00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:58.910
Mali's army-led goverment has expelled the
French ambassador and demanded the immediate

00:00:58.910 --> 00:01:03.800
departure of both French and European forces.

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:09.869
On the streets, the mood among the government's
supporters is clear.

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:18.460
"If France wants to leave, it must do so immediately,
no question of four or six months.

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:20.660
"We don't need France.

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:22.140
France has been with us too long!

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:24.680
Get her out!"

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:29.320
Popular resentment against France has been
driven by its failure to stem the tide of

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:31.320
radical Islamic attacks in Mali.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:37.210
The French troops' withdrawal now potentially
opens the door for talks between the government

00:01:37.210 --> 00:01:39.850
and radical islamist forces it opposes.

